+/* Sized for the conversation, not for one image.  A 1000-token image at the
+ * 2560-wide fp32 row width costs 10,240,000 bytes, so the old compile-time
+ * 128 MiB budget held 13 images.  An agent conversation that carries 15
+ * screenshots therefore could not fit its own working set, and because every
+ * request replays every image in history order, the LRU victim was always the
+ * next image that same request asks for: one over-capacity step turned into a
+ * full-set re-encode on every later turn (measured 2026-11-14, one session:
+ * 14 hits + 1 encode per turn up to 13,092 cached rows, then 0 hits and 15
+ * encodes per turn -- 79 s and 83 s of encoder time for a request whose model
+ * work was 1.5 s of prefill plus 22 s of decode).  The entry cap now matches
+ * the per-request image limit, and the byte budget is a runtime setting. */
+#define SERVER_IMAGE_CACHE_ENTRIES SERVER_MAX_IMAGES
+#define SERVER_IMAGE_CACHE_DEFAULT_MB 1024u
